A||||10||Mach10||Chassis flex||||5||
Z||000000||Mach10||12-21-2001||01:09 PM||||I know that my frame flexes a little on cornering. I can hear the sunroof creak... I know that the front-end (at least) isn't as robust as it probably should be. Has anyone ever fabricated, or found a source for any equipment that would help this? Something like strut tower braces, only mounted to the frame rails? I'd be interested in finding out... I'm pretty sure it probably isn't as simple as hard-bolting a couple of aluminum bars to the frame... Or would it? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||12-21-2001||01:39 PM||||I believe the sunroof creak is from the whole unibody flexing. Adding whatever bracing the convertible conversions are using should stiffen it up.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Mach10||12-21-2001||01:49 PM||||So, that's a wrought I-beam X under the car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Only about 500lbs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||12
Z||000003||ray b||12-21-2001||08:58 PM||||see if you can find a exploded drawing of the IMSA first gen of racers<BR>they used a full cage plus braces to supention's pickup points for less twist<BR>but unless you want to roadrace<BR>it is not needed and extra weight<BR>will slow the car more than it is worth.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||ITB 2M4||12-22-2001||12:25 AM||||The ones in IMSA were full out tube frame racecars with the 90 degree V-6 de-stroked to 3.0 litres in GTO and the Super Duty in GTU.  Now, the 8 pt. roll cage I have in my car.....  Just totally strip out the interior, use an aluminum seat, and you should be under your original weight.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||1
