Z||000008||cadero2dmax||12-22-2001||04:57 AM||||I have several friends in the SCCA that have cages in their daily drivers. <P>The absolute only drawbacks: <BR>(1) you are adding weight, and that weight is pretty high. A cage has the tendency to increase the overall height of your center of gravity, (which doesn't help handling)<BR>and <BR>(2) Damn, a full cage makes the Fiero difficult to get in and out of - especially the passenger with that damn Petty bar across their lap - - <P>There is a little flex on the Fiero, but after racing mine for the past (almost) decade I can tell you it is nominal flex compared to other marque's; I have had no stress cracks that I ever found, for example - except the typical sail panel cracking.<P>I had a cage in mine for the first couple years, but when I went from GT racing where it is required to Solo where it is not, I removed it. And I can tell you the car is more nimble and drives better with out that weight.<P>G<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Texas_Motor_Speedway_3.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by cadero2dmax (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||12-24-2001||05:27 AM||||The Fiero has a very strong and rigid frame, unless you have a modified-body (or, to a certin degree, T-top) car, I'd doubt you actually need more stiffness.<P>If by some odd stroke, you have a hardtop/sunroof (dosen't matter, they're the *exact* same chassis) Fiero that you still want to stiffen...<P>Get the same X-braces the convertible guys use.<P>Yes, they decrease ground clearance, and yes they add about 100lbs of weight.<P>But they're rigid.<P>IF that's what you really want.<P>I am considering it for my T-top car one day.  It still flexes less than an SLK Mercedes (which is NO sloppy chassis car by any measure) but I'd like to one day take out that middle bar and integrate it into the glass pannels, for a true 'GTS' Targra.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||rogergarrison||12-24-2001||07:02 AM||||My Ferraro is quiet and solid as a Cadillac compared to the Vette. It rattles and bangs like a semi-tractor.||||reg||1
